- public void nextPermutation(int[] nums)
- requires nums != null && nums.length >= 1 && nums.length <= 100 && (\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < nums.length; 0 <= nums[i] && nums[i] <= 100);
- ensures the permutation of nums is the lexicographically next greater permutation of numbers, or the lowest possible order if not possible
- ensures the replacement is done in place using only constant extra memory